  # ── Island - Atoll ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Low and broad, with the widest beach of the six: an exponent below 1 raises the
  # lowlands, so most of its area sits just above the waterline instead of climbing
  # away from it. Astern of the start — the island you find by turning round.
  #
  # Waterline at 0.400 of the height range (24 m of base below sea level over a
  # 60 m HeightScale); peak about 36 m above the water. The layer bands below are
  # anchored on that number, not on absolute heights, so every island bands the
  # same way in relative terms however deep it is sunk.
  - Entity: 879000000000007
    TagComponent:
      Tag: Island - Atoll
    TransformComponent:
      # Origin is a CORNER, not the centre: a 400 m tile centred on (330, ., -480).
